2. The use is Small Business Use.

"Small Business Use" means production use solely for the benefit of You and
Your Affiliates when the Combined Gross Revenue of You and Your Affiliates for
the immediately preceding fiscal year was less than USD 1,000,000. If You or
an Affiliate did not exist for a complete preceding fiscal year, use a
reasonable, good-faith projection of Combined Gross Revenue for the current
fiscal year.

"Affiliate" means an entity that directly or indirectly controls, is
controlled by, or is under common control with You. "Control" means ownership
of more than fifty percent of voting interests or the power to direct
management or policies by ownership, agreement, or otherwise.

"Combined Gross Revenue" means the worldwide gross revenue of You and all
Your Affiliates, consolidated without double counting and converted to United
States dollars using a reasonable and consistently applied exchange rate.
Revenue may not be separated by subsidiary, Affiliate, customer, deployment,
installation, or geography to qualify for this grant.

A consultant, managed service provider, reseller, or other service provider
may rely on this Additional Use Grant for production use on behalf of another
person or entity only when both the service provider's group and the ultimate
beneficiary's group independently qualify for the applicable Permitted
Production Use. This Additional Use Grant does not permit offering the Licensed
